monero: declare strsafe.h's functions in util.cpp instead of defining them.

0015 links the Windows library's winpthread statically, and with that the link
failed:

    libmingwex.a(lib64_libmingwex_a-strsafe.o): in function `StringCchPrintfA':
    multiple definition of `StringCchPrintfA';
    libcommon.a(util.cpp.obj): first defined here

mingw-w64 13's libwinpthread.a calls StringCchCopyNA, so its thread.o pulls
strsafe.o out of libmingwex.a. That object is built with __CRT_STRSAFE_IMPL
and carries an ordinary definition of every strsafe function. util.cpp includes
strsafe.h the normal way, which defines the same functions as extern "C"
__inline, and g++ emits the ones it uses as COMDAT copies. ld accepts any number
of COMDAT copies but not one alongside a plain definition. Linked against the
import library, as before, nothing pulled strsafe.o in.

__CRT__NO_INLINE is the header's own switch for this: it turns every function
into a plain declaration, so util.cpp calls the libmingwex definitions and
there is only one of each. It is defined around the one include only.
windows.h, stdio.h and string.h are already in by then and their include guards
keep them as they were, so nothing else in the file changes.

Only util.cpp includes strsafe.h in monero.

diff --git a/src/common/util.cpp b/src/common/util.cpp
index f3b39fe43..7fb3282fc 100644
--- a/src/common/util.cpp
+++ b/src/common/util.cpp
@@ -75,7 +75,12 @@ using namespace epee;
 #endif
   #include <windows.h>
   #include <shlobj.h>
+  // Declarations only: the definitions come from libmingwex, whose strsafe.o a
+  // static winpthread also pulls in. Inline copies here would be a second
+  // definition of each, which ld rejects.
+  #define __CRT__NO_INLINE
   #include <strsafe.h>
+  #undef __CRT__NO_INLINE
 #else 
   #include <sys/file.h>
   #include <sys/utsname.h>
